WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.610
In 2000, foreign firms invested 1.3
billion dollars directly in Vietnam.

2
00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:11.250
In 2024, the figure was
20.2 billion dollars.

3
00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:13.990
New factories, owned from abroad.

4
00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.240
A global company builds a plant.

5
00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.120
Local people get jobs.

6
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.830
But profits can flow back to
owners in another country.

7
00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:25.510
So when a global company builds
a factory in a poorer country,

8
00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:27.310
who really gains?

9
00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:30.070
In this mission, you'll weigh
up what foreign investment

10
00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:31.830
can bring a host country,

11
00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:33.820
and what it can take away.

12
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.970
Then you'll use a graph lab to see what

13
00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:38.030
new factories do to an economy,

14
00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:40.630
straight away and years later.

15
00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:44.230
Your mission: find out what
decides whether foreign investment

16
00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:46.990
really pays off for the
country that receives it.
